<title>POLAND: Polish minimum T-bill prices flat, benchmark down.</title>
<headline>Polish minimum T-bill prices flat, benchmark down.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of most Polish T-bills remained flat at today's primary auction on total demand of 1.21 billion zlotys against a 1.1 billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The treasury sold 669 million zlotys worth of the bills.  </p>
<p>   T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week 52-week</p>
<p>   new min price    --	95.46    91.12     --	83.47</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    --     (95.46)  (91.12)    --     (83.48)</p>
<p>   new max price    --	95.50    91.16     --	83.55</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    --     (95.52)  (91.17)    --     (83.70)</p>
<p>   offer		--	300.0    200.0     --	600.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded    --	561.3    160.6     --	488.5</p>
<p>   bids accepted    --	295.2     32.1     --	341.2</p>
<p>   next auction     --	300.0    200.0     --	600.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
